
1. Core Task Management

• TODO: The standard placeholder for future work, missing features, or planned optimizations.
• FIXME: Urgent issues that require immediate attention. It signifies that the code is currently broken, buggy, or failing and needs a developer to fix it.
• HACK: A temporary workaround. It alerts the team that the code is sub-optimal or "ugly" (often written quickly to meet a deadline) and should eventually be refactored properly.

2. Bugs & Security

• BUG: An active, known bug that has been identified in the code but hasn't been fixed yet.
• SECURITY: Vulnerabilities or security risks. This flags code that requires extra auditing, encryption updates, or compliance checks.

3. Documentation & Code Health

• UNDONE: A reversal or rollback of a previous feature. It notes that a change was reverted and needs to be handled properly.
• XXX: A warning flag. It warns other developers to look closely at a piece of code because something is tricky, unusual, or potentially problematic.
• NOTE / INFO: Important context. Unlike other tags, this isn't an action item; it simply highlights vital architectural or procedural information that another developer must read.